<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sentence of Guadalupe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1486">1486</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-remences">War of the Remences</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sentence of Guadalupe was an arbitral ruling issued by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon">Ferdinand II of Aragon</a> at the monastery of Guadalupe on 21 April 1486. It ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-remences">War of the Remences</a> by allowing Catalan remença peasants to redeem the 'evil customs' that bound them to their lords, and it abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> in Catalonia.</p></div>
